        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this exceptional second-floor three-bedroom apartment to the market, ideally positioned within the ever-popular Eaton development in the heart of Rathcoole, County Dublin.\nThree-bedroom apartments in Rathcoole are an exceptionally rare find, making No. 8 Eaton Way a truly unique opportunity. Extending to an impressive c. 135 sq.m, this stunning apartment is more than double the size of many properties within the Eaton development, offering an outstanding level of space that is seldom available in apartment living.\nPresented in superb condition throughout, the bright and spacious accommodation of c.134sqm comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, an expansive open-plan living, dining and kitchen area, three generous double bedrooms, two of which benefit from stylish ensuite bathrooms, a contemporary family bathroom, and a separate utility room. Further enhancing this remarkable home are two sunny private balconies, accessed from both the living area and the master bedroom, providing the perfect spaces to relax and unwind.\nThe location is second to none. Situated in the heart of Rathcoole Village, every conceivable amenity is within walking distance, including schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and local services. Excellent public transport links, including Dublin Bus, provide swift access to Dublin City Centre, while the nearby N7 and M50 make commuting even more convenient. A host of sporting and recreational facilities are also within easy reach.\nProperties of this calibre, size and location rarely come to the market. Early viewing is highly recommended.\nContact RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today to arrange a viewing.\n\nFeatures\n<ul>\n <li>3 bed, 3 bath</li>\n <li>Second floor apartment</li>\n <li>B Energy Rating/ Green Mortgage Potential</li>\n <li>135 sq.m</li>\n <li>Gas fired central heating</li>\n <li>Two private balcony's leading from both the lounge and master bedroom</li>\n <li>Highly sought-after development</li>\n <li>Designated parking</li>\n <li>A rare find!</li>\n <li>Fantastic location in the heart of Rathcoole village</li>\n <li>Extremely well-presented throughout</li>\n <li>Early viewing is highly advised</li>\n</ul>\n\nBER Details\nBER: B\n\nDirections \nEircode: D24 K5W4"
      },
